# local-only sites config (real device hosts never in the public repo; P2 decision 2026-10-19)
sites.toml
!examples/sites.toml
# operator-created deploy files, made by copying the tracked templates beside them and kept
# mode 0600 and out of git: gateclerk.env carries the site tokens, mnotify.toml the notify config. Named
# as exact paths rather than `*.env` so this rule can never shadow a tracked template or a
# future fixture; tests/test_deploy_templates.py pins both directions.
deploy/gateclerk.env
deploy/mnotify.toml
# The mnotify secret files (MICRO_NOTIFY_SECRETS=file reads one file per account here),
# never committed. `secrets/` at the top of this file matches a
# directory named exactly `secrets`, NOT this one. Anchored, and no trailing slash: a
# trailing-slash rule still catches the directory and a file under it, but misses the symlink
# an operator points at secrets stored elsewhere (measured — `git status` lists it). The
# prefix form also swallows a per-site variant created beside it, and
# tests/test_deploy_templates.py section 6 proves it shadows no tracked path.
/deploy/mnotify-secrets*
